\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\title{Fixed-budget trace-selection protocol}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{harness}

\p{The trace-selection intervention is a finite evaluation proposal. It
compares horizon and selector choices at a declared retained budget while
keeping the model, teacher, scaffold, task split, verifier, randomization law,
and cost coordinates visible. The selective-refinement study supplies the
comparison pattern; the typed interface, receipts, and estimators below are
FTIP adaptations rather than source results
\citet{Sections 6-7; Tables 4-5, 10}{dang2026selecting}.}

\p{The route separates the experiment interface
(\ref{ftip-00P8}), its receipt-derived quantities
(\ref{ftip-00P9}), and a finite paired calculation
(\ref{ftip-00PA}). No result is claimed until an implementation supplies the
declared receipts.}

\transclude{ftip-00P8}
\transclude{ftip-00P9}
\transclude{ftip-00PA}
